tributes":{},"children":["The best explainers translate without selling"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#journalists-ask-different-questions-than-builders"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["03"]},{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Journalists ask different questions than builders"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#the-translators-are-the-people-who-keep-nostr-from-sounding-smug"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["04"]},{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["The translators are the people who keep Nostr from sounding smug"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#a-good-explainer-changes-the-emotional-temperature"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["05"]},{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["A good explainer changes the emotional temperature"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#education-becomes-culture-when-it-repeats"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["06"]},{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Education becomes culture when it repeats"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#sources"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["07"]},{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Sources worth opening"]}]},"\n            "]},"\n          "]},"\n          ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-content"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"header","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-header"},"children":["\n              ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-meta"},"children":["\n                ",{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["People"]},"\n                ",{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["7 min read"]},"\n                ",{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Education"]},"\n              "]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{},"children":["Educators, Hosts and Writers Who Translate Nostr"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The best Nostr educators do not merely define keys, relays and clients. They make the reader feel less foolish while crossing from platform habits into protocol thinking."]},"\n            "]},"\n\n            ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-callout"},"children":["\n              ",{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["Reader route:"]}," Read this for the explainers, hosts, writers and journalists who help new people understand why Nostr is worth the trouble.\n            "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"education-is-not-a-side-quest"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["Education is not a side quest"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Nostr is difficult because it asks normal users to care about things platforms hid from them: keys, relays, clients, signing, zaps, lists, event kinds and backup habits. A good educator does not simply define those words. They sequence them. They know what a beginner needs now and what can wait. They know that frightening people with key loss in the first minute can be as harmful as hiding the risk entirely."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["This is why educators, hosts and writers belong in People. They are not decoration around the protocol. They are the bridge that lets the protocol recruit people who did not come from open-source or Bitcoin."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"the-best-explainers-translate-without-selling"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["The best explainers translate without selling"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A weak explainer turns Nostr into marketing: censorship-resistant, decentralized, user-owned, revolutionary. A strong explainer shows the tradeoffs. Yes, the identity model is powerful. Yes, clients are interchangeable in a way platform apps are not. Yes, relays give the network flexibility. Also yes, onboarding is rough, moderation is unresolved, key custody is scary and discovery can be uneven."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Readers trust educators who can hold both sides. That is why figures such as BTC Sessions, Daniel Prince, The Nostr Report, conference hosts and patient writers matter. They give newcomers a way in without pretending the hallway is finished."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"journalists-ask-different-questions-than-builders"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["Journalists ask different questions than builders"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Builders often explain how something works. Journalists ask who it affects, who benefits, who is missing, what went wrong and why a reader outside the scene should care. Nostr needs that pressure. A community that only listens to builders can become technically correct and socially unreadable."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Profiles of journalists, hosts and media people need to ask what audience they bring. A Bitcoin audience, a mainstream tech audience, a human-rights audience, a local meetup audience and a creator audience all hear Nostr differently. The translator matters because the listener changes the story."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"the-translators-are-the-people-who-keep-nostr-from-sounding-smug"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["The translators are the people who keep Nostr from sounding smug"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Nostr can sound smug when it is explained badly. \"Just own your keys\" is not a helpful answer to someone who has never managed identity outside a platform. The best educators understand that. They translate without humiliating the reader. They explain keys, relays, clients, zaps and signers in the order a person can absorb them. They admit what is still awkward. They make the network feel worth the trouble."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Derek Ross, BTC Sessions, ODELL, Lyn Alden, The Nostr Report, Plebchain Radio, Nostr Design contributors and many conference hosts play different versions of this role. Some teach setup. Some explain economics. Some report updates. Some host conversations. Some give designers and builders a language for onboarding. The shared value is that they make the scene less sealed off."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Education is not a side quest. It is how open protocols get a public."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"a-good-explainer-changes-the-emotional-temperature"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["A good explainer changes the emotional temperature"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The hardest part of Nostr education is not the vocabulary. It is the emotional temperature. New users can feel foolish, exposed or annoyed when asked to manage keys, choose relays and understand why one app does not show what another app shows. A good explainer lowers the temperature without hiding the truth. They make the reader feel capable."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["That is why the People hub should treat educators and hosts as central characters. They are the people who turn \"censorship-resistant social protocol\" into a morning routine, a first post, a safe signer habit, a podcast episode, a zapped musician, a conference room or a working client choice. The bridge is human before it is technical."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The best translation does not sell Nostr as finished. It makes the unfinished parts readable enough to enter."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n          ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section","id":"education-becomes-culture-when-it-repeats"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["Education becomes culture when it repeats"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The phrases a community repeats become culture. Not your keys. Relay choice. Zaps. NIP-05. Signer. Client. Public key. Web of trust. These words can invite or exclude. Educators shape whether the vocabulary becomes a ladder or a wall."]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The People hub needs to follow the people who make the ladder. They are often the difference between Nostr as a clever protocol and Nostr as a place a reader might actually enter."]},"\n          "]},"\n\n            ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-section crays-article-sources","id":"sources"},"children":["\n              ",{"tag":"h3","attributes":{},"children":["Sources worth opening"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"ul","attributes":{},"children":["\n",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://nostr.how/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener"},"children":["nostr.how"]}," - Beginner-friendly education site for keys, clients, relays and first use."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://nostr.report/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener"},"children":["The Nostr Report"]}," - Newsroom-style feed for releases, projects and community updates."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://plebchainradio.com/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener"},"children":["Plebchain Radio"]}," - Community audio and culture reference po